---
import PageLayout from '@layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@lib/site';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Terms', url: '/terms' },
];
const updated = 'May 28, 2026';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Use : Fortify AI by i-NETT"
  description="Terms of use for i-nett.ai. Acceptable use, intellectual property, disclaimers, and limitations of liability for use of the Fortify AI marketing website."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  pageHeading="Terms of Use"
  pageLead={`Last updated ${updated}. These terms govern your use of i-nett.ai. By accessing this site, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the site.`}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  hideFinalCta={true}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container-narrow legal">
      <h2>Scope</h2>
      <p>
        These terms apply to the i-nett.ai marketing site. Engagements with i-NETT for
        Fortify AI deployments are governed by separate written agreements, including a
        Master Services Agreement and any required Business Associate Agreement or Data
        Processing Agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>Use of the site</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to use the site lawfully and not to misuse it, including by attempting to
        gain unauthorized access, by interfering with site operation, or by using automated
        tools to scrape, harvest, or replicate the site beyond what is permitted by robots.txt
        and applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        i-nett.ai, the Fortify AI brand, the i-NETT brand, and all site content are the
        property of i-NETT or its licensors. You may quote, link, and reference our content
        for non-commercial purposes with attribution. You may not republish, redistribute,
        or commercially exploit site content without our written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party links and content</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to third-party content, including the HubSpot Meetings booking
        calendar and Apple Podcasts. We are not responsible for the content, terms, or
        privacy practices of third-party sites. Use of those services is governed by their
        own terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Informational use only</h2>
      <p>
        Content on the site is for general informational purposes. It does not constitute
        legal, financial, medical, regulatory, or compliance advice. For advice specific to
        your situation, consult qualified professionals.
      </p>

      <h2>No guarantees</h2>
      <p>
        Estimates produced by tools such as the ROI calculator are illustrative and are not
        guarantees of results. Actual results vary by industry, deployment scope, and
        execution. The site is provided on an &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as available&rdquo;
        basis without warranties of any kind to the maximum extent permitted by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, i-NETT will not be liable for any indirect,
        incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising out of your use of
        the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify and hold i-NETT harmless from any claim arising out of your
        misuse of the site or violation of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, without regard to
        conflict-of-law principles. Any dispute arising out of these terms or your use of the
        site will be resolved in the state or federal courts located in San Diego County,
        California.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date
        above will reflect any change. Continued use of the site after changes constitutes
        your acceptance of the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can be sent to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="disclaimer">
        These terms are informational and are not legal advice. For legal advice about how
        these terms apply to your situation, consult qualified counsel.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .legal h2 { margin-top: var(--space-7); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .legal h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
  .legal p { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
</style>
